The Barbarian wrote:
> Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanag...@hotmail.com> wrote:
>
>> I am curious what other players do strategically
>> to make such potential robe destroying events less likely, and what you
>> do in case that (robe destruction) happens. Robes are rare and killing a
>> temple priest probably not the preferred way to get a new one - or is it?

Once I leanred the price of killing a shrine priest and the effort
required to repay that cost, I took up killing the minetown priest in a
reasonable percentage of games.  On the way back up from mines end in
most cases.

>> Or do you try to reach the castle wand to wish for a new one?

I don't remember including a robe in my list of Castle wand wishes.

> How rare is a robe?  Would an armor shop usually have one?

The probability is listed as a 3.  For comparison the probability of a
teeshirt is listed as a 2.  It is not usual for an amor shop to have
either but it also not unusual to encounter a randomly generated one at
some point in non-speed games.

As with so many item types, when they are in the initial inventory of a
type of monster they are more common in games than their random chance
suggests.  Items with 0 probability can only be generated in a monster's
initial inventory or in a possibly guaranteed death drop like dragon
scales or worm teeth.  Because priests come with one of two very
valuable cloaks (as well as spellbooks) those items can seem to appear
in most games.


